how to build your own fan base to become  a successful musician in the old days  you had to be anointed are recognized by  gatekeeper usually a record label the  same was true for authors to be  successful your main goal was to  convince a publisher to take a risk on  you similarly visual artists needed  galleries and radio host needed stations  talent wasn't enough in other words even  if you had a proven means of providing  something valuable to an audience you  still had to rely on the powers that be  to help you reach that audience  fortunately times have changed in the  world of stardom today thanks to mediums  like Instagram and Twitter that make  engaging and communicating with fans  easier than ever more and more people  are carving out a space for the  independent fans supported work indie  musicians often choose to go it alone  even after they had the opportunity to  sign with labels traditional publishers  are now scrambling to sign authors who  have sold hundreds of thousands of books  directly to readers to Amazon's Kindle  platform for sometimes even directly to  their own websites the musicians artists  and writers who fly out today understand  that their success is due not only to  the fans which is something that artists  have always said the difference is that  now success is due to the relationship  with artists maintained with the fans  almost without exception those who  succeed in the new economy share for  specific characteristics a body of work  product of ABBA fans the audience a  means of sharing the body of work the  platform and a way of getting paid for  their work the money none of these four  requirements is optional you need all of  them to succeed in the new economy it  can be tempting to cherry-pick an  example of someone famous who's made it  big by emitting something listed above  but those are the very rare exceptions  if you're hoping to follow the proven  model you need all four requirements  [Music]
 

